// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
// synth_ethereal.ys — documented Yosys flow for the eLUT4 netlist (E0-MAP1).
// The Python runner (synth_ethereal.py) is the canonical entry point; this .ys
// documents the identical flow for transparency / manual use:
//
//   yosys -s synth_ethereal.ys
//
// (Substitute <design> / <out_prefix>; the runner does this programmatically.)
//
// Each `$lut` cell (WIDTH=4) in the output IS one eLUT4: its truth table maps to
// the eLUT4 `tt` field. `$dff` cells map to the eLUT4's integrated FF at bitgen.

// read_verilog <design>
// synth -auto-top
// abc -lut 4          // 4-input LUT mapping via ABC
// opt -full
// clean
// stat                // area report (eLUT4 count)
// write_json <out_prefix>.json
// write_blif <out_prefix>.blif
